WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:20.640
Open the demo sales alert to review its regional explanation.

2
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:31.520
South revenue fell 29.1 percent; the whole business moved 5.8 percent.

3
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:42.840
The $16,144 South revenue drop is explained by Online and Wholesale drivers.

4
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:52.280
The workflow checks each figure before keeping the AI explanation.

5
00:00:52.280 --> 00:01:03.800
The demo alert board holds the explanation for Sales Ops.

6
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:24.560
Typed by Claude (automated test) as Sales Ops: open a request.

7
00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:44.400
Typed by Claude (automated test) as Sales Ops: check this date.

8
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.520
Saving the request starts the sales check.

9
00:01:48.520 --> 00:02:38.400
The workflow calculates the day against its comparison window.

10
00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:46.760
This normal day finishes the check quietly.

11
00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:56.340
The normal-day route stays quiet.

12
00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:02.700
Sales Ops opens a demo alert for review.

13
00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:20.980
The search brings the returns alert into view.

14
00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:32.140
The returns movement is ready for Sales Ops review.

15
00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:38.260
Typed by Claude (automated test) as Sales Ops: mark the alert Not material.

16
00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:41.700
Saving keeps the feedback with the alert.

17
00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:42.980
The workflow recounts the alert feedback.

18
00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:49.860
The feedback board brings the reviewed alerts together.

19
00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:57.420
The demo alerts keep their recorded materiality decisions.

20
00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:15.860
Typed by Claude (automated test) as the analyst: open the rule.

21
00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:22.020
Typed by Claude (automated test) as analyst: threshold 0.3 becomes 0.7.

22
00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:25.540
Saving makes the revised rule available to the next check.

23
00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:32.540
The automated setup requests another check through MCP.

24
00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:46.380
The workflow brings the new check into view.

25
00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:51.580
The revised threshold leaves this sales day quiet.
